cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Boolean Algebra over Trapdoor Sets: A Practical Framework for Privacy-Preserving Set Operations with Probabilistic Guarantees"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Towell
    given-names: Alexander
    email: atowell@siue.edu
    affiliation: "Southern Illinois University Edwardsville"
repository-code: "https://github.com/queelius/boolean-algebra-over-trapdoor-sets"
abstract: >-
  A framework for privacy-preserving set operations built from cryptographic
  trapdoors. A trapdoor set holds opaque, deterministic element trapdoors and
  supports a collision-bounded generalized Boolean algebra (union and intersection
  negatives) while answering membership as a plaintext boolean by byte-equality.
  It never recovers plaintext; what it exposes is the equality predicate among
  ciphertexts (the deterministic-encryption / searchable-encryption leakage
  profile), trading that leak for set operations whose only error is a hash collision.
keywords:
  - cryptographic hash functions
  - trapdoor data structures
  - privacy-preserving computation
  - approximate algorithms
  - probabilistic data structures
  - Bernoulli types
license: MIT
